{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA (rebar-debug Phase 1, confirmed at runtime)\n\nMECHANISM. The `Git version floor gate` step in .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml\n(introduced by 980d, merged c433663721) reads .github/git-version-floor.txt from the\nCHECKED-OUT TREE and hard-errors when absent:\n\n    floorfile=.github/git-version-floor.txt\n    if [ ! -f \"$floorfile\" ]; then\n      echo \"::error::missing $floorfile (the single source of the Git version floor)\"\n      exit 1\n    fi\n\nGerrit's Verified lane takes the workflow DEFINITION from the target branch but checks out\nthe CHANGE'S tree, so any change branched before c433663721 gets the step without its data\nfile and fails hard, regardless of what the change touches.\n\nDISCRIMINATING EXPERIMENT (runtime, not static). Parsed the live step out of the workflow\nYAML and executed its `run:` script under bash against two temp trees:\n  - tree WITHOUT .github/git-version-floor.txt -> exit 1, '::error::missing ...'\n  - tree WITH the file                          -> exit 0, 'declared floor: git >= 2.38;\n                                                   runner has git 2.55.0'\nThat splits the two candidate explanations (tree-skew vs. a genuine under-floor runner):\nthe runner's git is 2.55.0, far above the 2.38 floor, so the failure is caused solely by\nfile absence.\n\nLEGITIMACY: defect. The authoritative source is in this very file, lines ~136-152, the\n'Definition-vs-tree skew guard (ticket ee2a)' note, which states verbatim: 'New gate steps\nthat run a repo script must copy this if-present guard: skip (with a log line) when the\nscript is absent from the checked-out tree; the gate re-enforces on rebase and on every\npost-merge change.' Two adjacent steps (raw-git-write gate, wall-clock-assert gate) already\nimplement it. The floor gate violates the documented invariant.\n\nFIX PLAN. Apply the established if-present pattern, keyed on the floor file, so an absent\nfloor file skips with an explanatory log line naming WHY (change predates the gate; it\nre-enforces on rebase / post-merge) instead of erroring. 980d's real enforcement is\npreserved unchanged: an under-floor git still fails with required version, installed\nversion and upgrade path, and tests/conftest.py's session-abort is untouched.\n\nCALLER SWEEP. The gate step is CI-only. The other floor consumers (tests/_git_floor.py,\ntests/conftest.py pytest_configure, docs) read the file directly and are unaffected. The\nexisting pins test_ci_reads_the_floor_from_the_single_source (workflow must name the floor\nfile) and test_consumers_declare_the_same_floor (workflow must name 2.38) both still hold."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785910908303258001,"uuid":"1f8ae1a3-97c9-417b-8425-8e42d0c9d99c"}